<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Álvaro II of Kongo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1587">1587</a>–<a href="/years/1614">1614</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Álvaro II Nimi a Nkanga</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Álvaro II Nimi a Nkanga was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-kongo">Kongo</a> from 1587 to 1614 and one of its most powerful and important kings. He succeeded his father Álvaro I after a dispute with his brother, settled by single combat at M'banza-Kongo (São <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador">Salvador</a>) to avoid bloodshed. After a poorly documented civil war in 1590–91 he had to accept the virtual independence of Miguel, count of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soyo">Soyo</a>, and rewarded loyal nobles with habits of the Order of Christ, which Kongo kings went on granting through the 19th century. In 1596 M'banza-Kongo became the seat of a diocese, though the kings of Portugal chose its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishop</a>, and in 1604–1608 he sent Emanuele Ne Vunda as ambassador to Pope Paul V.</p></div>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbanza-kongo">M'banza-Kongo</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/angola">Angola</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mbanza-kongo">M'banza-Kongo</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/angola">Angola</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=-6.27,14.25&amp;year=1600" aria-label="M'banza-Kongo on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4945 2398 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Álvaro II of Kongo"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5395 2668h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5395 2668h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=-6.27,14.25&amp;year=1600">What was here in 1600? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
